# Frontend styling and theme

Applies to all UI work under `frontend/`. Build/API pairing rules live in `.cursor/rules/frontend-tsc-gate.mdc`.

## Stack constraints

- **Plain CSS only** — no Tailwind, CSS-in-JS, or Sass unless explicitly requested.
- **Global theme tokens** in `frontend/src/App.css` (GitHub Primer palette).
- **Component styles** in a co-located `ComponentName.css` imported from the matching `.tsx`.
- **Reuse shared shells** from `App.css` when they exist (`.modal-*`, `.app-header`, tab chrome, etc.).

## Night / day mode (required on every UI change)

This UI supports **dark** (default, "night") and **light** ("day") modes. Every new or changed surface must be readable in **both**.

| Mechanism | Detail |
|---|---|
| React state | `App.tsx` — `useState<'dark' \| 'light'>` |
| DOM hook | `document.body.dataset.theme` = `'dark'` or `'light'` |
| Persistence | `localStorage` key `scaleai-theme` |
| Bootstrap | `main.tsx` applies saved theme on `body` (and `html` when light) before React mount |
| Toggle | Header button — label "Day" in dark mode, "Night" in light mode |

Components that need the active theme in JS (canvas, particles) read `document.body.dataset.theme` or receive a `theme` prop — see `LandingPage.tsx`, `ParticleBackground.tsx`.

## CSS token contract

**Do not hardcode** `#…`, `rgb(…)`, `rgba(…)`, or named colors (`white`, `black`, `gray`) for backgrounds, text, or borders in component CSS. Use variables from `App.css`.

| Token | Use for |
|---|---|
| `--bg`, `--bg-inset` | Cards, inputs, page shell |
| `--surface`, `--surface-2` | Elevated panels, secondary fills |
| `--border` | Borders, dividers, table rules |
| `--text`, `--text-muted` | Primary and secondary copy |
| `--accent`, `--accent-hover` | Links, highlights, emphasis |
| `--error`, `--error-text`, `--error-bg`, `--error-border` | Error and danger states |
| `--radius` | Border radius (6px) |

Dark values live on `:root`. Light overrides live in **`body[data-theme='light']`** in `App.css` only — not duplicated per component file.

### Correct pattern

```css
.my-panel {
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.my-panel select {
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}
```

Tokens flip when the user toggles theme. **Do not** add redundant blocks like:

```css
/* WRONG — restates the same vars for both themes; delete these */
body[data-theme='dark'] .my-panel { color: var(--text); }
body[data-theme='light'] .my-panel { color: var(--text); }
```

If contrast breaks in one mode, fix the **token** in `App.css` or pick a different token — do not patch one theme with a literal hex in the component file.

### Wrong patterns (reject)

- Literal colors on surfaces or text in component CSS (`#ffffff`, `rgb(15, 23, 42)`).
- Assuming light mode (e.g. white panel + `#333` text) without tokens.
- Inline `style={{ background: '#…' }}` for theme-dependent UI — use a class + `var(--…)`.
- Copy-pasting dark-theme rgba values from chart components into form/panel CSS.

### When literals are allowed

Only for **data visualization** accents that cannot map to a shared semantic token (timeline bars, latency histogram fills). Prefer:

1. Add a named token pair to `App.css` (`:root` + `body[data-theme='light']`), or
2. Read tokens at runtime — `LatencyTimeline.tsx` / `LatencyStats.tsx` use `getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--…')`.

## Contrast checklist (before handback)

1. Toggle **Day / Night** in the app header — no invisible text, borders, or same-tone foreground+background.
2. **Form controls** (`input`, `select`, `textarea`, native `button`): `color: var(--text)` on `background: var(--bg)` or `var(--surface)`; border `var(--border)`.
3. **Helper / placeholder copy**: `var(--text-muted)`, not a one-off gray.
4. **Errors**: `var(--error-text)` or `var(--error)`; error panels use `var(--error-bg)` + `var(--error-border)`.
5. **Tables and lists**: header and cell text `var(--text)`; row borders `var(--border)`.
6. **Modals**: extend `.modal-card` / `.modal-backdrop` from `App.css`; do not invent a parallel modal skin.

Run `rg '#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}|rgb\\(|rgba\\(' frontend/src/components/YourComponent.css` — hits must be zero unless documented as chart-only.

## Tests

Vitest files live under **`frontend/tests/`** (not co-located under `frontend/src/`). `vite.config.ts` includes `tests/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}`.

| Concern | Where |
|---|---|
| DOM / RTL outcomes | `frontend/tests/App.test.tsx`, `frontend/tests/JsonTree.test.tsx`, `frontend/tests/ServicesPage.test.tsx` |
| Both themes render content | `it.each(['dark', 'light'] as const)` + `document.body.dataset.theme = theme` before `render()` — add under `frontend/tests/` when the surface needs it |
| CSS uses tokens not literals | Static read of the CSS file in a `frontend/tests/*.test.ts(x)` — assert key selectors contain `var(--text)` / `var(--bg)` and no literal `color:` / `background:` hex |

When adding a component CSS file with themed surfaces, add that token test in the same change.

